        <item>
            <title>1.5</title>
            <pubDate>Mon, 03 Aug 2026 23:21:10 -0700</pubDate>
            <sparkle:version>2608032320</sparkle:version>
            <sparkle:shortVersionString>1.5</sparkle:shortVersionString>
            <sparkle:minimumSystemVersion>15.0</sparkle:minimumSystemVersion>
            <description><![CDATA[<h2>LiveManager 1.5</h2>

<p>Switching looping off now sticks.</p>

<h3>Fixed</h3>
<ul>
  <li><strong>Looping stays off.</strong> Turning the loop off and moving to
      another demo used to bring the brackets straight back, and any demo you'd
      ever pressed ⌘L on would re-loop itself every time it played. Off now
      means off — on that demo, on the next one, and after a relaunch.</li>
  <li>The loop button still remembers where you left the brackets, so switching
      looping back on picks up the section you were working on rather than
      starting from the ends of the demo.</li>
</ul>

<p>One-time note: the first time you open 1.5, every demo starts unlooped. Your
bracket positions are all still saved — one press of ⌘L on a demo brings its
section back.</p>

<h3>Also since 1.3</h3>
<ul>
  <li><strong>Logic Pro support.</strong> Logic projects appear as songs
      alongside your Ableton sets, with tempo, time signature, track count and
      alternatives listed as versions.</li>
  <li><strong>Volume slider</strong> in the player bar, remembered between
      launches.</li>
  <li>A repeated project file could crash the app on launch; LiveManager now
      repairs the duplicate instead of stopping.</li>
</ul>
]]></description>
