        <item>
            <title>1.4</title>
            <pubDate>Mon, 03 Aug 2026 16:50:32 -0700</pubDate>
            <sparkle:version>2608031649</sparkle:version>
            <sparkle:shortVersionString>1.4</sparkle:shortVersionString>
            <sparkle:minimumSystemVersion>15.0</sparkle:minimumSystemVersion>
            <description><![CDATA[<h2>LiveManager 1.4</h2>

<p>Logic Pro projects now sit alongside your Ableton sets.</p>

<h3>New</h3>
<ul>
  <li><strong>Logic Pro support.</strong> Point LiveManager at a folder containing
      Logic projects and they appear as songs, with tempo, time signature, track
      count and the version of Logic that saved them — rated, tagged and filed
      into albums just like Ableton sets.</li>
  <li><strong>Alternatives become versions.</strong> Each of a Logic project's
      alternatives is listed under Versions, newest first, so you can see when
      each was last saved.</li>
  <li><strong>Bounces are found automatically.</strong> Logic keeps bounces and
      recorded takes in the same folders, so LiveManager ranks them: audio named
      after the project, or sitting in a Bounces folder, is offered first — a
      stray loop or take won't hijack the demo slot.</li>
  <li><strong>Volume slider</strong> in the player bar, remembered between
      launches.</li>
</ul>

<h3>Fixed</h3>
<ul>
  <li>A repeated project file could crash the app on launch, with no way back in.
      LiveManager now repairs the duplicate instead of stopping.</li>
  <li>"Open in Ableton" now says Logic when the song is a Logic project, and opens
      the project rather than a file inside it.</li>
</ul>
]]></description>
