        <item>
            <title>1.2</title>
            <pubDate>Sat, 01 Aug 2026 16:02:50 -0700</pubDate>
            <sparkle:version>2608011601</sparkle:version>
            <sparkle:shortVersionString>1.2</sparkle:shortVersionString>
            <sparkle:minimumSystemVersion>15.0</sparkle:minimumSystemVersion>
            <description><![CDATA[<h2>LiveManager 1.2</h2>

<p>This version adds automatic updates — from here on, LiveManager can update
itself in one click instead of you re-downloading it.</p>

<h3>New</h3>
<ul>
  <li><strong>Automatic updates.</strong> LiveManager checks for new versions in
      the background, or on demand from <em>LiveManager → Check for Updates…</em></li>
  <li><strong>Waveforms.</strong> The player bar draws the demo's waveform, so you
      can see the arrangement while you listen.</li>
  <li><strong>Loop a section.</strong> Hit the loop button (⌘L) and drag the
      brackets to cycle any part of a demo. Loop points are remembered per song
      and sync to the iPhone app.</li>
  <li><strong>iPhone companion.</strong> Listen to your library and set loop points
      on the go — see <em>Help → Get the iPhone App…</em></li>
</ul>

<h3>Improved</h3>
<ul>
  <li>A warning now appears if iCloud sync isn't working, instead of failing
      silently.</li>
  <li>Song details are aligned and easier to scan; notes have room to breathe and
      commit when you click away.</li>
</ul>
]]></description>
